cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its benchmark, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Industrial AI Guardian: fault and integrity monitoring for the transmitters behind industrial soft sensors"
authors:
  - given-names: Tejas
version: 0.2.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tejascodz/industrial-ai-guardian"
abstract: >-
  A monitoring layer that tells transmitter faults (and which transmitter)
  apart from process faults, operating-regime changes and data-integrity
  attacks in a closed-loop process, and keeps a soft-sensor estimate usable
  while a transmitter is faulty. It combines a bank of per-tag virtual
  sensors with a reconstruction test, closed-loop fault signatures,
  instrument and integrity checks and DCS setpoint context, and is
  benchmarked against limit checks and PCA baselines on a closed-loop
  Tennessee Eastman simulation and on the HAI 21.03 hardware-in-the-loop
  dataset.
keywords:
  - process monitoring
  - fault detection and diagnosis
  - sensor validation
  - soft sensor
  - Tennessee Eastman process
  - industrial control system security
  - OPC UA
